    {
      "id": "claim_0371d0314190490db1e351252913aabc",
      "statement": "The canonical-home rule routes a durable learning by the concept's front matter: a concept carrying a `resource` is a derived summary so the learning goes into the cited source, while a concept with no `resource` is authoritative and listed under `authoritative:` in the protection manifest so the learning goes into the concept; the governance gate enforces the classification in both directions (G11) and rejects an authoritative concept whose policy is `regenerate` (G12).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/wiki-maintenance.md#L516-L552",
